WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.462
Welcome to How to Grow Cassava. In this lesson, you will learn how to choose a good place to plant.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:11.420
Cassava grows best in loose soil that drains well. Roots need room to swell.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:17.034
Choose land that does not stay flooded after rain. Standing water rots the roots.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.894
The field should get sun for most of the day.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:25.424
Pick a place you can reach easily for weeding, harvesting and carrying produce.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:28.087
Avoid swampy or low-lying land.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.627
Avoid very stony or hard, compacted ground.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.295
And avoid fields where diseased cassava grew last season.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:44.372
Before you move on, check: Walk the land after rain. Squeeze the soil: it should crumble. Check for sun most of the day.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.210
In the next lesson: Healthy stems make healthy plants.
